NVIDIA proprietary graphics driver 615.71.09 (R615 driver branch) for the
Gaming Live CD.

Scope after the true Arch-style split (this same .run is also unpacked by
Nvidia-Utils, and later by Lib32-Nvidia-Utils / Nvidia-Settings):

- Kernel modules built against the Linux 7.2.5 kernel that ships on the CD:
  nvidia, nvidia-modeset, nvidia-drm, nvidia-uvm, nvidia-peermem, installed
  into /Programs/Linux/Current/lib/modules/<release>/kernel/drivers/video so
  they appear under /lib/modules on the CD.
- The Xorg DDX: nvidia_drv.so and libglxserver_nvidia.so.615.71.09.
- The GSP + ucode firmware blobs, installed to
  /lib/firmware/nvidia/615.71.09/ (they ship here permanently: a separate
  linux-firmware-nvidia package would do nothing but re-copy these four files
  from this same .run).
- Transitionally: the nvidia-settings binary + .desktop + icon. This moves to
  its own recipe (Nvidia-Settings) as the split is completed.

The userspace libraries, command-line tools, Vulkan ICDs, glvnd EGL vendor
JSONs, OpenCL ICD, udev rule, modprobe blacklist and Xorg OutputClass are
shipped by Recipes/Nvidia/Nvidia-Utils.

Install notes:
- The kernel modules are compiled during the recipe build against
  /Programs/Linux/Current/lib/modules/<release>/build, so the Linux package
  must be installed on the build system first (step order: linux, then nvidia).
- 615.71.09 needs NO source patches on Linux 7.2.5: NVIDIA's own conftest
  detects the drm_atomic_state -> drm_atomic_commit rename (Linux v7.2) and
  the CRTC/plane atomic_check argument change, and the strscpy conversion is
  already done upstream. (580.159.04 needed three sed patches; do not copy
  them here.)
- depmod must run inside the chroot; running `depmod -b <rootfs>` from the
  host destroys the chroot-absolute symlinks under /System/Index/lib/modules.
